# Who is asked to review what. See GOVERNANCE.md.
#
# Each project profile has one slot for a profile reviewer: a person who works
# on that project and checks its facts. Until a reviewer takes a slot, the line
# names the maintainers. Do not leave a line with no owner: GitHub then treats
# the file as having no code owner at all. To take a slot, open a pull request
# that adds your handle to the line, and add your affiliation to MAINTAINERS.md
# in the same pull request.
#
# GitHub requests a review from the owners of a file when a pull request is
# ready for review (not while it is a draft). Branch protection decides whether
# that review is required. When it is required, an approval from any one owner
# on the line is enough. GitHub ignores an owner with no write access to this
# repository.

